    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n42084" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">rūta</span></b> , ae, f., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥυτή</span> (cf. <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, § 103</span></i>
		Müll.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				bitter herb</i>, <i>rue.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam.
				9, 22, 3</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Col. 11, 3, 38</span></i>; <i><span class="en">12, 7, 5</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 19,
				8, 45, § 156</span></i>; <i><span class="en">20, 13, 51, §
			131</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. R. Am. 801</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Mart. 11,
				31, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">52,
			8</span></i>.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			
			<b>Trop.</b>, <i>bitterness</i>, <i>unpleasantness</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cras exspecto Leptam, ad cujus rutam pulegio
					mihi tui sermonis utendum est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fam. 16, 23, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
